00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:14,880
got with the rotor on top, which is always spinning,

508
00:33:14,881 --> 00:33:16,280
really acts like a parachute.

509
00:33:16,580 --> 00:33:18,120
So even if you lose an engine,

510
00:33:18,320 --> 00:33:20,980
even if you're 10 feet off the ground or 50 feet or whatever,

511
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:24,000
you've got a built-in parachute that's going to bring you down

512
00:33:24,001 --> 00:33:25,840
and land safely and softly.

513
00:33:28,600 --> 00:33:32,740
The Carter Copter is a so-called slowed rotor compound design.

514
00:33:33,460 --> 00:33:36,780
The large composite rotor blade has heavily weighted tips,

515
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:39,000
whose pitch is controlled by the pilot.

516
00:33:40,060 --> 00:33:43,340
On takeoff, the rotor is spun at high speed.

517
00:33:43,341 --> 00:33:46,140
Then the pilot increases the pitch.

518
00:33:47,600 --> 00:33:50,420
The rotor's inertia quickly lifts the aircraft off the ground.

519
00:33:51,740 --> 00:33:53,940
To make the transition to fixed wing flight,

520
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,600
a pusher propeller engages as the rotor slows

521
00:33:57,601 --> 00:33:59,540
and uses the wind stream to keep it turning,

522
00:34:00,160 --> 00:34:01,640
decreasing the drag on the aircraft.

523
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:08,460
For decades, aviation buffs dreamt of the flying car.

524
00:34:08,461 --> 00:34:14,600
In 1945, Robert Fulton Jr. took flight in his Air Fibian,

525
00:34:15,380 --> 00:34:18,040
the first certified roadable aircraft,

526
00:34:18,580 --> 00:34:21,820
meaning it could both fly and operate legally as an automobile.

527
00:34:22,640 --> 00:34:25,460
The vehicle could hit a top speed of 55 on the ground

528
00:34:25,461 --> 00:34:27,560
and 110 in the air.

529
00:34:28,980 --> 00:34:32,340
But the most famous winged automobile was the AeroCar,

530
00:34:32,940 --> 00:34:35,980
first built by Moulton Taylor in 1949.

531
00:34:38,460 --> 00:34:41,460
Taylor built three versions of the aircraft,

532
00:34:41,560 --> 00:34:45,460
with the third reaching a flight speed of 135 miles per hour.

533
00:34:48,700 --> 00:34:50,700
So what's our status here on this right here?

534
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:52,300
This has been given heavy.

535
00:34:52,400 --> 00:34:54,700
Jay Carter has already begun construction

536
00:34:54,800 --> 00:34:57,220
on a four-seater version of his aircraft,

537
00:34:57,320 --> 00:35:00,220
known as the Foreplace.

538
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:04,220
A super lightweight, rigid body is crucial to its success.

539
00:35:04,320 --> 00:35:07,920
This is the fuselage for our Foreplace Personal Airbus.

540
00:35:07,921 --> 00:35:10,420
It's actually made in two parts that come apart.

541
00:35:10,421 --> 00:35:12,920
And I'll show you here how we pull this apart.

542
00:35:15,920 --> 00:35:17,920
The aircraft itself is actually completed.

543
00:35:17,921 --> 00:35:21,920
The inside of the fuselage is actually this part right here,

544
00:35:21,921 --> 00:35:23,920
inside of the mold.

545
00:35:23,921 --> 00:35:26,920
And it's actually made in a composite construction.

546
00:35:26,921 --> 00:35:30,920
And it's basically a layer of honeycomb with one layer of carbon

547
00:35:30,921 --> 00:35:31,920
on either side of it.

548
00:35:31,921 --> 00:35:34,920
And it makes for an extremely strong, lightweight structure.

549
00:35:34,921 --> 00:35:38,663
lightweight structure. In fact, this is what the honeycomb looks like.

550
00:35:38,664 --> 00:35:40,000
It's just paper honeycomb

551
00:35:40,001 --> 00:35:44,163
impregnated with resin. This is what the carbon fiber looks like.

552
00:35:44,164 --> 00:35:46,020
It's only 10,000-some-an-inch

553
00:35:46,021 --> 00:35:48,152
thick, just a little bit thicker than your hair.

554
00:35:48,153 --> 00:35:50,240
Once you impregnate that with resin and bond it

555
00:35:50,241 --> 00:35:54,720
on, now you've got a structure where this right here is lighter than aluminum and stronger than

556
00:35:54,721 --> 00:35:58,694
steel. Extremely efficient way to build an aircraft.

557
00:35:58,695 --> 00:36:01,140
But Carter's slowed rotor design

558
00:36:01,141 --> 00:36:03,600
It certainly isn't the only way for a winged aircraft

559
00:36:03,601 --> 00:36:05,740
to achieve vertical liftoff.

560
00:36:05,741 --> 00:36:11,160
In 2005, the US Marines began flying the V-22 Osprey,

561
00:36:11,161 --> 00:36:12,980
an aircraft that can quickly ferry troops

562
00:36:12,981 --> 00:36:14,320
to pinpoint locations.

563
00:36:18,800 --> 00:36:21,820
The Osprey is a tilt rotor, meaning its propellers

564
00:36:21,821 --> 00:36:24,180
engage downward for helicopter-like thrust

565
00:36:24,181 --> 00:36:27,840
during takeoff and then rotate forward

566
00:36:27,841 --> 00:36:30,340
to become turboprops.

567
00:36:30,341 --> 00:36:32,000
like a standard prop-driven aircraft.

568
00:36:35,980 --> 00:36:38,940
At Bell Helicopter in Arlington, Texas,

569
00:36:38,941 --> 00:36:42,880
the Bell Augusta 609 is the world's first civilian tilt

570
00:36:42,881 --> 00:36:43,581
rotor.

571
00:36:47,400 --> 00:36:53,400
The 609's wingspan is 34 feet, and the prop rotor spans 60 feet.

572
00:36:53,401 --> 00:36:56,600
The maximum airspeed is 316 miles per hour.

573
00:36:56,601 --> 00:37:01,100
It's a unique aircraft.

574
00:37:01,101 --> 00:37:07,560
It's the only commercially developed aircraft that can take off and land vertically and

575
00:37:07,561 --> 00:37:14,980
fly up to 25,000 feet, more than 300 miles an hour, in pressurized comfort, land 700

576
00:37:14,981 --> 00:37:17,420
miles away vertically again.

577
00:37:17,421 --> 00:37:22,060
So it really is a new way to fly.

578
00:37:22,061 --> 00:37:26,500
And you have a power lever here and you have a center stick.

579
00:37:26,501 --> 00:37:31,980
And just like in a helicopter with a collective, you pull up on this power lever and the aircraft

580
00:37:31,981 --> 00:37:35,220
will just come straight up in the air.

581
00:37:35,221 --> 00:37:38,300
The immediate thing you feel is acceleration.

582
00:37:38,301 --> 00:37:41,240
It actually kicks you back in your seat a little bit.

583
00:37:41,241 --> 00:37:48,540
And you start accelerating, start climbing out at a rather dramatic rate, I might add.

584
00:37:48,541 --> 00:37:51,840
The 609's purpose is point-to-point travel.

585
00:37:51,841 --> 00:37:56,240
It speeds twice that of the fastest helicopter.

586
00:37:56,241 --> 00:38:00,140
With seating for up to nine passengers in a luxury cabin,

587
00:38:00,141 --> 00:38:02,900
it's a business commuter's dream.

588
00:38:02,901 --> 00:38:05,500
Integrating three onboard flight computers,

589
00:38:05,501 --> 00:38:08,840
designers built the 609 with safety and efficiency in mind.

590
00:38:12,540 --> 00:38:15,540
Despite its precise avionics and controls,

591
00:38:15,541 --> 00:38:18,640
pilots in training require a few sessions in the flight simulator.

592
00:38:21,840 --> 00:38:25,840
But who should apply for the captaincy?

593
00:38:25,940 --> 00:38:29,780
Helicopter pilots or airplane pilots?

594
00:38:29,880 --> 00:38:33,880
If you're a helicopter pilot, it flies just like any other

595
00:38:33,980 --> 00:38:37,180
helicopter when you pick it up to a hover.

596
00:38:37,280 --> 00:38:40,400
And as an airplane pilot, when you turn it into an airplane,

597
00:38:40,500 --> 00:38:44,200
you'd be very comfortable and ride it home as an airplane.

598
00:38:44,300 --> 00:38:46,640
In the not-so-distant future,

599
00:38:46,740 --> 00:38:51,040
the 609 tilt rotor and a handful of personal air vehicles

600
00:38:51,041 --> 00:38:53,640
could become the extreme convenience aircraft

601
00:38:53,740 --> 00:38:54,940
for the casual traveler.

602
00:39:00,940 --> 00:39:04,980
Another extreme aircraft is hard at work fighting fires.

603
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:09,100
This modified jumbo jet is king of the aerial fire trucks.

604
00:39:13,300 --> 00:39:17,740
Between 2000 and 2005, a NASA program sometimes

605
00:39:17,741 --> 00:39:21,040
sometimes called the highway in the sky,

606
00:39:21,041 --> 00:39:22,980
developed navigation technologies

607
00:39:22,981 --> 00:39:25,980
for the projected future when personal air vehicles

608
00:39:25,981 --> 00:39:28,560
filled the skies.

