00:39:32,521 --> 00:39:34,120
here on the History Channel.

611
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:42,460
We now return to Extreme Aircraft II on Modern Marvels.

612
00:39:47,740 --> 00:39:59,780
In 2006, more than 96,000 fires charred nearly 9.9 million acres

613
00:39:59,781 --> 00:40:05,300
in the United States and cost a record $1.5 billion to fight.

614
00:40:05,301 --> 00:40:07,860
With human life and property at stake,

615
00:40:07,861 --> 00:40:09,660
having the right fire truck is critical.

616
00:40:09,661 --> 00:40:16,660
In Victorville, California, a converted DC-10 passenger jet

617
00:40:16,661 --> 00:40:21,660
called the 10-Tanker Air Carrier claims the title of world's

618
00:40:21,661 --> 00:40:24,660
heaviest firefighting jet.

619
00:40:29,660 --> 00:40:33,660
The 10-Tanker weighs in at 400,000 pounds fully loaded.

620
00:40:33,661 --> 00:40:38,660
The wingspan is 150 feet, and max airspeed is 440 feet.

621
00:40:38,661 --> 00:40:42,900
Air speed is 460 miles per hour.

622
00:40:42,901 --> 00:40:45,940
We're looking at the tank system, external free tanks

623
00:40:45,941 --> 00:40:48,760
that carry a lot of fluid, 12,000 gallons,

624
00:40:48,761 --> 00:40:50,940
aerodynamic tank on each end.

625
00:40:50,941 --> 00:40:54,000
The technology was bought from Ericsson Air Crane,

626
00:40:54,001 --> 00:40:56,540
comes out through a computer-controlled door

627
00:40:56,541 --> 00:40:59,440
down at the bottom, gives you the flow rate you want

628
00:40:59,441 --> 00:41:02,420
so that you get the coverage level you need on the ground.

629
00:41:02,421 --> 00:41:04,960
As you can see, they're hitched to the airplane

630
00:41:04,961 --> 00:41:07,780
with some very heavy structure.

631
00:41:07,781 --> 00:41:11,620
The airplane itself had to be modified so that that structure

632
00:41:11,621 --> 00:41:14,980
could bolt into a load carrying area of the airplane.

633
00:41:14,981 --> 00:41:18,260
The airplane was designed to have most of the weight inside.

634
00:41:18,261 --> 00:41:22,500
We've transferred a lot of the weight outside.

635
00:41:22,501 --> 00:41:25,460
The tanks are filled with either water or fire retardant.

636
00:41:28,740 --> 00:41:32,780
The retardant is simply water mixed with nitrogen,

637
00:41:32,781 --> 00:41:35,380
an effective fire suppressant that's slow to evaporate.

638
00:41:37,780 --> 00:41:42,380
Because the liquid is a dense 9.3 pounds per gallon,

639
00:41:42,480 --> 00:41:46,960
a full 12,000-gallon load weighs in at a staggering 60 tons.

640
00:41:51,600 --> 00:41:56,100
Getting that hefty payload air buoy requires immense thrust.

641
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:58,760
We've got three engines, each of which develop

642
00:41:58,860 --> 00:42:02,140
40-some thousand pounds of thrust.

643
00:42:02,240 --> 00:42:06,080
And at the weights we're flying, in this case,

644
00:42:06,081 --> 00:42:08,580
in this case, under 400,000 pounds,

645
00:42:08,680 --> 00:42:11,280
you get a very favorable thrust to weight ratio,

646
00:42:11,380 --> 00:42:13,080
even with a full load of retardant,

647
00:42:13,180 --> 00:42:15,080
which exceeds 100,000 pounds.

648
00:42:19,100 --> 00:42:21,760
The 10 tanker is the newest heavy lifter on the scene.

649
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:27,500
But for the past half century, a wide assortment

650
00:42:27,600 --> 00:42:31,000
of aerial fire trucks has shouldered the load.

651
00:42:31,100 --> 00:42:33,580
That included many surplus World War II bombers

652
00:42:33,581 --> 00:42:37,220
and transports converted to firefighters in the late 1940s.

653
00:42:41,520 --> 00:42:45,720
By the 1960s, a variety of tanker aircraft built specifically

654
00:42:45,721 --> 00:42:47,120
to bite fires took over.

655
00:42:49,700 --> 00:42:52,300
Helicopters using buckets that could refill quickly

656
00:42:52,301 --> 00:42:55,000
from lakes or reservoirs became a favorite tool

657
00:42:55,001 --> 00:42:56,300
in the wildfire wars.

658
00:42:56,301 --> 00:42:58,300
ports.

